From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:11:30 -0700
Subject: [dawn][vk] Allow querying and filtering on Vulkan device/driver
 UUIDs.

Two new chained structs are added in VulkanBackend.h (because it is not
possible to declare a uint8_t[VK_UUID_SIZE] in dawn.json), with
additions to ChainUtilsImpl and tests.

 - AdapterPropertierVulkanUUIDs returns the device/driver UUIDs when
   chained in an AdapterInfo.
 - RequestAdapterOptionsVulkanUUIDs filters the returned adapters to
   return only the ones with matching device/driver UUIDs.

Other small changes are:

 - ChainUtils.h STypeFor is fixed to support extensions in ChainUtilsImpl
   for out structs.
 - VulkanDeviceInfo member names are aligned to all end with
   "Properties".

Bug: 563358700
Change-Id: I19231b0a77f97e3d62ffcaa6eed32d609c099427
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/347715
Reviewed-by: Loko Kung <lokokung@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y): dawn.json on this branch ends the
SType enum at value 81 (no "render bundle encoder resource table",
"dawn shader source SPIRV" or "shared buffer memory host pointer
descriptor" entries yet); the two new entries were added with their
upstream values 85 and 86 after entry 81. AdapterBase::ValidateGetInfo()
does not exist on this branch, so the AdapterPropertiesVulkanUUIDs
feature check was added next to the existing AdapterPropertiesVk check
in AdapterBase::APIGetInfo() using the branch's
mInstance->ConsumedError(DAWN_VALIDATION_ERROR(...)) form. All other
hunks (VulkanBackend.h, ChainUtils, BackendVk, PhysicalDeviceVk,
TextureVk, VulkanInfo rename, tests, docs) applied verbatim, except
that this branch has no src/utils/span.h (no ByteSpanFromRef /
Span::CopyFrom helpers, added upstream by
https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/319855), so the
VK_UUID_SIZE byte copies were written with std::ranges::copy /
std::copy_n (PhysicalDeviceVk.cpp PopulateBackendProperties and the
AdapterEnumerationTests.cpp VulkanUUIDs test, which also hashes the
seed with the branch's Sha3_256::Hash(const void*, size_t) overload
and includes <algorithm>). This Dawn change reached chromium/src
through the roll
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8532290.

